# Two loads of the rule page, as the two containers logged them (docker compose logs -t frontend api-service),
# sorted by time. nginx logs a request when it finishes, so each API line comes just before the nginx line
# for the same call. Captured 15 Oct 2026 in desktop Chrome, the same session as ../ui-calling-backend.png.
#
# 23:38:50 first load: nginx serves the page (200), its CSS and its script; the script calls
#          /api/rules/EPA-HQ-OW-2022-0801/sections, nginx forwards it to api-service as /rules/..., the API answers 200.
# 23:39:02 the reload (Cmd+R) before the screenshot: the page is a 304 (browser cache, unchanged), and its
#          CSS and script come from the cache without a request, but the API call is made again.
#
# frontend lines are nginx's access log (the browser address 192.168.65.1 is Docker Desktop's gateway).
# api-service lines are uvicorn's; 172.18.0.3 is the frontend container on the compose network.
